Send a binary file's response headers before its body when gzip is skipped.

Image and PDF previews in the file viewer, and file downloads, answered
"Error loading file: 500" (omnigent-ai/omnigent#10481). The server image
resolves Starlette 1.8.0, not the 1.3.1 in uv.lock. For a binary read or a
download the handler calls skip_gzip(), and _StateAwareGZipResponder set
Starlette's content_type_is_excluded on the first body message. Starlette
1.8.0 no longer sends the start message it held back on that path, so the
body went out first and a request with Accept-Encoding: gzip, as every
browser sends, failed with "Received http.response.body without
http.response.start".

Backports the _gzip_route.py change from upstream PR #10585: the responder
reads the flag on http.response.start and passes the start and every body
message through unchanged. Takes three of that PR's tests; the responder
test fails without the fix on Starlette 1.3.1 too. The PR's download proxy
hardening is left out.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0017-codex-bypass-default.patch.
